WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.140
Consider the
following experiment.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.780
You have two pieces of
metal, copper and zinc,

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.980
which you connect
to conducting wires.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.340
And you then submerge the
metals in an electrolyte,

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:15.310
in this case vinegar.

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:26.560
You will observe that bubbles
will form around the zinc

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.390
but not on the copper.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:32.340
The metals seem
dissimilar in this way.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.550
And if you then connect the
two wires holding the metals,

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.070
something changes.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:41.370
Tiny bubbles begin to form
around the copper terminal.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:44.560
It seems as though something
is being pulled from the zinc

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.440
through the wire,
allowing a reaction

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.710
to occur on the copper side.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:53.430
And it turns out this is a
flow of electrical charge,

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:56.400
as electrons are pulled
away from the zinc

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:02.580
towards the copper through the
conductive path in the wire.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:06.350
Think of this flow as the
result of a charge imbalance,

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.510
or electrical pressure
between the two metals.

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:12.960
As compared to the
instantaneous discharge

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.446
observed with static
electricity experiments.

00:01:17.446 --> 00:01:20.210
And towards the end
of the 18th century,

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.790
Alessandro Volta had been
investigating this effect.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.510
More importantly, he found
that chaining these cells

00:01:26.510 --> 00:01:32.080
together would amplify
this flow of charge.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:34.940
And by 1800, he simplified
things even further,

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:37.740
removing the jar, which
provided more electrolyte

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.300
than was actually needed.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.210
He writes, "A few dozen
small round disks of copper,

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:47.700
pieces of coin for example, and
equal number of plates of zinc,

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.450
I prepare circular
pieces of spongy matter

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:52.420
capable of retaining water.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.770
I continue coupling a plate
of copper with one zinc,

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:58.250
and always in the same
order, and interpose

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.780
between each of these
couples a moistened disk.

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.060
This continues until I
have a column as high

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.680
as possible without
danger of it falling."

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:11.360
This is known famously as the
voltaic pile, the first battery

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.350
in history to provide
a continuous flow

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:17.690
of electrical charge or current.

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:20.760
More cells resulted in an
increased electrical pressure

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.430
at the two ends, and
electrical pressure

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:27.920
was an early term for what we
now call voltage, after Volta.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.750
Now if the two leads
of a voltaic pile

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.980
were brought into direct
contact, a series of shocks

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.690
could be observed.

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:40.040
Now at first, the utility
of electric current

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:43.710
as a communication method was
not immediately obvious, aside

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:46.240
from faint sparks and bubbles.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.990
One idea was to use the presence
of bubbles to signal letters,

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:53.810
and the bubble telegraph
used this method,

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:58.180
though it involved 26 different
circuits, one for each letter.

00:02:58.180 --> 00:03:00.490
And it was based on the fact
that the battery providing

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.000
the current can be placed at
a distance away from the jars

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.940
containing the leads
creating the bubbles.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.961
An inventive, although
clumsy system,

00:03:08.961 --> 00:03:09.960
which was never adopted.

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.920
But very soon,
everything changed

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.105
after a famous
demonstration in 1819.

00:03:18.105 --> 00:03:22.730
It was found that if we simply
pass a wire near a compass

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:27.110
and connect it to a battery, as
soon as the wire made contact

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.530
with the battery,
the needle jumped

00:03:29.530 --> 00:03:32.790
without any physical contact.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.020
The only explanation was that
the current-carrying wire

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:40.150
was creating a temporary
magnetic field.

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:42.360
This was followed
by a series of tests

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.620
to figure out the
direction of this field.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:49.560
First we assumed it was pointing
along the wire with the current

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:52.460
or perhaps emanating
outwards from the wire,

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:53.460
as heat would travel.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.000
But eventually, it
was deduced that it

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:06.520
must be traveling around the
wire in perpendicular circles.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.870
So a loop of wire would
create a magnetic field,

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:12.900
which points through
the center of the loop

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.165
and around the outside.

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:20.019
This led to the
galvanometer, which

00:04:20.019 --> 00:04:24.316
was designed to detect and
measure electrical current.

00:04:24.316 --> 00:04:26.680
And it was just
simply a coil of wire

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.700
with a compass
suspended in the center.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:39.980
Now when electric current
was applied to the coil,

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:43.160
a magnetic field would push
through the middle of the coil

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:45.080
and around the outside.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:47.580
So the needle would
always point perpendicular

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.570
to the direction
of the force, which

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:52.670
was balanced on either
side of the needle.

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:55.880
And the stronger the current,
the stronger the deflection

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.410
of the needle.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.960
And by 1824, William
Sturgeon demonstrated a way

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.450
to increase the strength
of this field even more.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.930
Simply by wrapping
a coil of wire

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:10.870
around a piece of
iron, such as a nail,

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.740
the magnetic force
could be amplified,

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:16.660
because iron seemed to be a
better medium for supporting

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:19.090
the formation of
magnetic fields.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.670
We call this permeability.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.090
And by wrapping the
wire many times,

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.300
the strength of the
field could be amplified

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:29.440
thousands of times, and this
is known as an electromagnet.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:36.120
So suddenly, it was possible
to create magnetic fields which

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.310
could move needles
with precision

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:43.530
and force using electric
current applied at a distance,

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:47.526
using a long loop of wire
and a strong battery.

00:05:47.526 --> 00:05:50.350
At the time, our
understanding of information

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.920
was in its infancy.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:55.060
People were thinking about
information in a message,

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:58.580
and as the number of
letters in a message.

00:05:58.580 --> 00:05:59.910
So the goal was intuitive.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:01.820
Who could come up
with the fastest way

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:04.100
to transmit letters?

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.820
And whoever had
the fastest system

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.510
would therefore reduce
the cost per message

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.340
for the sender
using this system.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:17.210
And a gold mine was waiting
for whoever got there first.

